You are working on an Astro project for a STEM education platform.

Project rules:

- Use Astro (.astro) for pages and layouts
- Use components for reusable UI (Header, Footer, etc.)
- Each page MUST use a layout
- Each layout MUST support SEO props: title, description, schema, url

SEO rules:

- Always include unique title and meta description per page
- Always include canonical URL
- Always include Open Graph tags (og:title, og:description, og:image)
- Always include Twitter card

Structured data (JSON-LD):

- WebSite and WebPage must be included globally in BaseLayout
- Use BreadcrumbList on all pages
- Use Article schema for educational content
- Use LocalBusiness + FAQ for instruction pages
- Use VideoObject for video pages
- Use WebApplication for calculator pages

Code style:

- Keep code minimal and clean
- Avoid unnecessary client-side JS
- Prefer server-side rendering (Astro default)
- Use client:visible only when needed

Routing:

- Use dynamic routes for cities and subjects (/instrukcije/[grad]/[predmet])
- Use slug-based routing for articles (/matematika/[slug])

Performance:

- Lazy load images
- Use semantic HTML (main, section, article)
- Keep layouts reusable

Images:

- Always use modern formats (AVIF, WebP)
- Always provide fallback using <picture>
- Always include loading="lazy"
- Optimize image size and resolution

Do not:

- Do not duplicate SEO logic across pages
- Do not hardcode URLs without base domain
- Do not skip schema implementation